    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nfiles\n\n### Description\n\nWhen you limit maximum number of windows to some small number and open mini.files for the directory of current file which is nested on a level grater than the max number of windows is, binding for reveal_cwd (@) won't work.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Set option `windows.max_number` to 2 and enable preview\r\n2. Open mini.files for your current file which is deeply nested in the project hierarchy\r\n3. Try to navigate to cwd using `mappings.reveal_cwd` binding (by default @)\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nmini.files opens cwd in focused window\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nmini.files does nothing and remains in the current directory",
